WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.560
Marvel's Doctor Strange had the enormous task
of introducing big magic to the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.560
Universe.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.780
You know, same reality as Captain America
and Iron Man and other science-based heroes.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.320
Even Scarlet Witch is explained as using "cosmic
energy" when she does her thing, so Doctor

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.200
Strange explores some weird new places for
our heroes.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.680
And fans and critics agree that it does so
really, really well.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.880
But despite having a compelling story and
mind-blowing visuals to boot, the film still

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.570
had a few head-scratchers that you just can't
wave a magic wand at.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.449
Here are a few plot points that not even Steven
Strange could explain.

00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:34.489
Missing magicians

00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:38.219
When Strange is going through his training
in Kamar-Taj, there are a boatload of other

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:42.899
would-be wizards taking on the same drills
and learning the same magic alongside him.

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:47.050
It's a whole wizard army, just ready to be
set loose on any mystical threats, ranging

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.480
from Kaecilius to David Blaine.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.799
So...where were all these folks when Kaecilius
attacked the Sanctums?

00:00:52.799 --> 00:00:57.379
The Ancient One knows that the bad guy is
going to try and take out the Sanctums.

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:00.699
So why is only one dude hanging out all by
himself as a defender?

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:05.950
They have the numbers to set up a platoon
of wizards at each Sanctum in case of an assault,

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:09.200
even if those trainees don't yet have full-on
magic mojo yet.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.360
A lack of training has never stopped fellow
baldy Professor X from throwing kids at the

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.530
bad guys.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.750
It's never stopped Batman.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.430
And it shouldn't have stopped an all-out war
against Kaecilius.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.710
Only the Surface

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.380
Like most big blockbusters, Marvel movies
have never been afraid of clunky product placement.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.970
Just ask everyone in Civil War about their
weird Vivo phones.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:33.280
In Doctor Strange, things are a bit more subtle,
but one noticeable little moment sticks out

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.280
like a sore thumb.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.950
Strange is a world-renowned doctor, and he's
pretty dang rich because of it.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.310
He doesn't skimp on the cars that he haphazardly
drives around mountains, and his extravagant

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.250
New York City apartment must cost millions.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.060
So, why does Stephen Strange use a Surface
3 tablet?

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.140
The Surface 3 is basically the Toyota Corolla
of the computer world.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.090
It's fine, but it's far from the best if you
have an unlimited budget.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.470
Strange couldn't even spring for a Surface
Pro?

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.350
That's weak stuff, Doc.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.350
Chain gang

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:04.590
The movie kicks off with Kaecilius stealing
spells from the library at Kamar-Taj in order

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.350
to summon Dormammu.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.200
It's clear that these books are extremely
dangerous … and they're only protected by

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.519
some … loose chains?

00:02:12.519 --> 00:02:16.939
It's basically Level One wizard stuff to make
a portal, so it's clear that the chains aren't

00:02:16.939 --> 00:02:18.299
there for protection.

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:22.130
That's why they have librarians … which
seems to be the most dangerous job in the

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.130
whole joint.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:27.040
After the initial head-chopping scene, we
see our man Wong in the library, protecting

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.040
the books.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:35.500
Unfortunately, Wong isn't, y'know, great at
his job.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.480
Technically, no knowledge is forbidden in
Kamar-Taj.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.650
But would it be so crazy to protect these
books a little better?

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:47.829
Obviously, a regular vault wouldn't be immune
to wizard portals, grabby hands, or even your

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:49.000
standard Hamburglar.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.980
But these guys have the most powerful magic
on Earth at their disposal!

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.870
There's gotta be a magic force field spell
in one of these books, right?

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.760
Sometimes the honor system just doesn't work,
okay?

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.329
Deus ex magica

00:03:01.329 --> 00:03:06.430
It's hard to overlook the film's most absurd
coincidence: Doctor Strange dives into a book

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:11.620
alllll about time manipulation — only moments
before Kaecilius attacks.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.249
It's perfect timing in the worst possible
way.

00:03:14.249 --> 00:03:17.959
Where the heck has Kaecilius been during all
this time while Strange is training?

00:03:17.959 --> 00:03:21.930
Kaecilius steals the pages for his spell in
the first moments of the movie, then waits

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.209
months to stage his next attack.

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:29.019
All he did was allow the Ancient One more
time to plan, train Strange, and beef up their

00:03:29.019 --> 00:03:30.029
defenses.

00:03:30.029 --> 00:03:32.540
Which ... they kind of failed at anyhow.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:33.909
Time and time again

00:03:33.909 --> 00:03:39.760
Mordo spends most of the movie warning Strange
over and over about messing around with time,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.809
noting it can result in everything from the
end of the world to severe constipation.

00:03:43.809 --> 00:03:47.260
"Temporal manipulations can create branches
in time.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.690
Unstable dimensional openings!

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:50.690
Spacial paradoxes!

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:51.690
Time loops!"

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:57.620
But later Strange uses the Eye of Agamotto
to rewind downtown Hong Kong to a time before

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:00.809
the local sanctum falls, in an effort to save
the day.

00:04:00.809 --> 00:04:05.849
He then cleverly mucks around with a time
loop to stop Dormammu in his tracks.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:06.849
"Dormammu!

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:09.799
I've come to bargain.

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:10.799
Dormammu!

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:11.799
Dormammu!

00:04:11.799 --> 00:04:12.799
Dormammu!"

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:16.850
If messing around with an apple was dangerous,
you'd think erasing the destruction of an

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:21.000
entire city is flirting with all-out cosmic
disaster, right?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.310
But after all those warnings from Mordo, there
are no immediate consequences for Strange's

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.530
actions.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.780
Everything seems...fine.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.050
Even still, Mordo seems to know what's up…

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:35.700
"You still think there will be no consequences,
Strange?

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.860
No price to pay?"

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:42.280
… but let's see Infinity War try to write
itself around legit time travel.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.420
Magic Mordo-torium

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.170
By the end of the film, Mordo's got a brand
new bag.

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:50.800
His new mission is to go around and take magic
away from people who use it, since too much

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.880
unchecked magic honestly seems like a pretty
bad idea.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.320
So, Mordo can apparently just take away magic
now?

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.170
That ability sure would've come in handy a
bit earlier.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.170
Y'know.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:05.340
When the dude with all the magic power was
straight up trying to end the entire world.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.880
Unless of course, Mordo can only suck the
magic out of low-level Dumbledores, like the

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.380
guy with the spine problems… which is a
pretty crappy magic trick.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.140
It's the magic equivalent of stepping on bugs:
I mean, it's pointless, and it only feels

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:19.380
good if you're a jerk.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.480
Mordo should pick on someone his own power
level.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.330
Guess we'll have to wait for Doctor Strange
II: Magic House Call for that.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.620
Thanks for watching!

